{"context":"eka status today is workspace-global (shows 7 projects regardless of cwd). Users working inside a repository (e.g., eka-cli) expect repo-local relevance. Execution state currently lives in .eka/execution-state.md (git-ignored, not canonical, not synced) — separate proposal adr:037 covers its CKO migration. This ADR decides the status scoping contract so status can later surface the execution-state CKO as 'current state only'.","decision":"When eka status runs inside an EKA repository (eka.yaml present + registered + synced), it shows only that repository's project + its repos and their last syncs (repo-scoped projection). Outside any repo, it keeps global behavior. Add --all flag to force global even inside a repo. Add --json machine output for scripts. MCP status tool mirrors same rule. Status surfaces execution-state CKO's current snapshot (latest instanceVersion) — not full history — via a new 'Execution' section.","consequences":"Positive: noise reduction, per-repo relevance, aligns status with view's project-union model, enables cross-device consistency when paired with execution-state CKO. Negative: breaking change for scripts expecting global output; requires migration (add --all). Neutral: MCP status tool must mirror same scoping logic.","alternativesConsidered":"1) Client-only render filter in cmd/status.go (cheapest); 2) Workspace.Status(repoFilter) server-side param with MCP parity; 3) Flag-only --repo/--project without auto-detection; 4) Keep global default + add --all to force global when auto-scoped. Chosen: (2) + (4) hybrid: auto repo-scoped inside EKA repo, global fallback outside, explicit --all overrides.","status":"proposed"}